{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanMarkovTrace"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.borromean_frobenius_reconstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.borromean_frobenius_reconstruction","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.lean#L74-L83","doc":"**Frobenius reconstruction (B).** The per-representation Jones sum\n`Σ_λ y_λ · χ^λ(β_Bor) = y_sym·1 + y_{(2,1)}·χ^{(2,1)}` equals the proved\nBorromean Markov-trace closed form `trM_borromean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.jones_markov_normalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.jones_markov_normalization","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.lean#L65-L72","doc":"**Markov normalisation.** `(y_{(3)}+y_{(1³)}) + 2·y_{(2,1)} = 1`,\ni.e. `Σ_λ y_λ d_λ = 1` with `d_{(3)}=d_{(1³)}=1`, `d_{(2,1)}=2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.hsq_add_four_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.hsq_add_four_pos","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.lean#L62-L63","doc":"`h² + 4 > 0` over ℚ (reused denominator non-vanishing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.chi21_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.chi21_borromean","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.lean#L58-L60","doc":"The standard-irrep character of the Borromean braid,\n`χ^{(2,1)}(β_Bor) = 2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶` (the one-dim characters are `1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.yJones_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.yJones_sym","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.lean#L54-L56","doc":"Sum of the two one-dimensional Jones–Frobenius weights,\n`y_{(3)} + y_{(1³)} = (h²+2)/(h²+4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.yJones_21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.yJones_21","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanFrobeniusReconstruction.lean#L51-L52","doc":"Jones–Frobenius weight of the standard (2,1) irrep: `1/[2]_q² = 1/(h²+4)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}